@startuml
title Implemented WebSocket keyword search

actor User
participant "Web UI / CLI" as Client
participant "SearchWebSocketHandler" as WS
participant "cached WebSocket executor" as Pool
participant SearchService
participant InvertedIndex

User -> Client: enter query; choose keyword
Client -> WS: connect /ws/search
Client -> WS: {requestId, query, mode: "keyword"}
WS -> Client: started(requestId, timestamp)
WS -> Pool: submit search task
Pool -> SearchService: search(SearchRequest, listener)
SearchService -> SearchService: validate query and capture State
SearchService -> InvertedIndex: search each normalized term
InvertedIndex --> SearchService: document ID sets
SearchService -> SearchService: merge, score and create snippets
SearchService -> WS: listener.keywordSearch(resultCount)
WS -> Client: keyword_search(requestId, resultCount)
SearchService -> WS: listener.done(SearchResponse)
WS -> Client: done(requestId, REST-compatible results)

note right of SearchService
Keyword mode skips Ollama and
query_expansion. Each request has
its own requestId and asynchronous task.
end note
@enduml
